    "created_at": "2020-10-21T15:29:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-10-21T15:33:24Z",
    "body": "That may lead to a great topic about how to protect sites from being modified unexpectedly via HTML mechanisms. Similarly, if we want to implement screen lock on a site, I hope that the lock mask is unable to be removed by removers if locked. Accessibilities of DOM nodes will give us a huge favour. In such a case without this feature, I need to do much more complicated jobs like detaching DOM nodes behind the lock mask into memories via some APIzl, so that users can not easily access the hidden nodes, and trying to recover them after unlocked.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
